solution:
**Given:**

How much does one have to add to dfrac{4}{5} to obtain dfrac{5}{4}?

**Formula used:**

Let x be the required number to be added.

dfrac{4}{5} + x = dfrac{5}{4}

**Calculation:**

dfrac{4}{5} + x = dfrac{5}{4}

⇒ x = dfrac{5}{4} - dfrac{4}{5}

⇒ x = dfrac{(5 times 5) - (4 times 4)}{4 times 5}

⇒ x = dfrac{25 - 16}{20}

⇒ x = dfrac{9}{20}

**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**
